# Data Protection (Backend)

## Purpose

Handle sensitive data responsibly across storage, transit, and logs.

## Classification

| Class | Examples | Handling |
|-------|----------|----------|
| Public | Product names | Standard |
| Internal | Internal IDs | Access control |
| Confidential | Email, phone | Encrypt at rest if required; minimize collection |
| Restricted | Passwords, tokens, CPF | Hash/encrypt; never log; strict access |

## Storage

- Passwords: bcrypt/Argon2 only — never reversible encryption.
- PII fields: collect minimum necessary; document retention policy.
- Encrypt sensitive columns at rest when compliance requires (project key management).

## Transit

- TLS everywhere — no sensitive data over plain HTTP.
- Validate SSL in outbound HTTP clients (don't disable cert verification).

## Logs & Errors

- Redact PII in logs (mask email: `j***@example.com`).
- No full request bodies in production logs by default.

## Deletion & Retention

- Support user data deletion requests when product requires GDPR/LGPD.
- Soft-delete vs hard-delete per domain rules — document in spec.

## Backups

- Treat backups as sensitive — same access controls as primary DB.
- Never restore production backups to unsecured environments.